# U8 (MODEL-FUZZY, I13): the open menu keeps the marked model by its id when a
# revalidated catalog lands under a ranked search (modelMenuDisplayIndex and
# hydrateMenuSnapshot, src/core/app/model_cache_runtime.zig:318-338,1121-1146
# @481104fd; fx's own case, :2086-2123). Every catalog read answers 4 s after
# it is asked. The launch's read is waited for (`first`); the second `/model`,
# past the 5 s revalidation floor, lists the first catalog at once and asks
# again, and `gpt5` and Down mark openai/gpt-5, second of three (`before`).
# The second catalog adds acme/gpt5-pro, which has `gpt5` as typed and so
# ranks first: the mark stays on openai/gpt-5, now third (`after`), and Enter
# uses it (`enter`). Both binaries show acme/gpt5-pro once it lands, so the
# `until` waits on that and not on a count.
fx: env FX_AUTO_UPGRADE=0
models p5-input-model-rank.json
modelsdelay 4000
wait 2
type /model
key Enter
until shown Models 7  [All]
wait 0.5
snap first
key Escape
wait 6
models2 p5-input-model-rank2.json
type /model
key Enter
wait 0.5
type gpt5
key Down
wait 1
snap before
until shown acme/gpt5-pro
wait 0.5
snap after
key Enter
wait 1.5
snap enter
gwlog
